<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Serbia</h1><p class="st-meta">1882 CE – 1918 CE · capital Belgrade</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Serbian kingdom that doubled its territory in the Balkan Wars, endured the First World War and became the core of Yugoslavia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan-i-of-serbia">Prince Milan Obrenović</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-serbia">Principality of Serbia</a>, independent since 1878, proclaimed himself king in 1882 with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>. His reign brought defeat by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-slivnitsa">Slivnitsa</a> in 1885 and domestic unrest, and he abdicated in 1889 in favour of his son Alexander.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The unpopular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-obrenovic">Alexander Obrenović</a> was murdered with his queen by army officers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia">May Coup</a> of 1903, and Peter I Karađorđević became king. Under the 1903 constitution and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-pasic">Nikola Pašić's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-radical-party">Radical Party</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> became a parliamentary state, freed itself from Austrian economic control after the Pig War of 1906, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> of 1912 to 1913 gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar-macedonia">Vardar Macedonia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a> assassination, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> attacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> in 1914. Overrun in 1915, its army retreated through <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corfu</a> and returned via the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-front">Salonika front</a> in 1918. On 1 December 1918 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a>, then called the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-serbia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Serbia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Paula · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Serbia_(1882%E2%80%931918).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1882 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Belgrade</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Milan I, Alexander Obrenović, Peter I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Serbian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, <a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kraljevina Srbija</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=kingdom-of-serbia" aria-label="Kingdom of Serbia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5168 594 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Serbia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5488 850L5501 875M5488 850L5380 747M5488 850L5488 850M5488 850L5459 926M5488 850L5503 821"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5501 875h0M5380 747h0M5488 850h0M5459